.TH MADEIRA-AOL 1 "2026-11-24" "madeira-aol 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
madeira-aol \- forward PC keyboard, mouse, and gamepad input over LAN to Madeira
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B madeira-aol
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIHOST\fR[\fI:PORT\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B madeira-aol
captures local raw keyboard, mouse, and gamepad events on Linux or Windows
and streams them with low latency over UDP (\fBMAOL\fR v1) to Madeira running
on iOS or iPadOS, while applying XInput controller vibration (rumble) feedback
returned from Madeira. It automatically reconnects across game switches and
app restarts and persists pairing keys locally so regenerated PINs do not
interrupt reconnection.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-discover
Probe the local network for Madeira instances and exit.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target =\fIADDR\fR
Connect directly to \fIHOST[:PORT]\fR instead of auto-discovering.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port =\fIPORT\fR
UDP port used for discovery and default target port (default: 37419).
.TP
.BR \-\-pin =\fIPIN\fR
Pairing PIN configured in Madeira's Accessories Over LAN settings.
.TP
.BR \-\-pair
Force fresh PIN pairing and overwrite any saved key for the target.
.TP
.BR \-\-forget
Remove the saved pairing key matching the target host or device ID and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-key\-file =\fIPATH\fR
Override the paired keys JSON path (defaults to user config directory).
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-reconnect
Exit when the remote session disconnects instead of auto-reconnecting.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-keyboard ", " \-\-no\-mouse ", " \-\-no\-gamepad
Disable forwarding for the corresponding input class.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-grab
Do not exclusively grab keyboard and mouse devices on Linux.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-rumble
Ignore rumble feedback packets sent by Madeira.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit discovery results as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-\-color =\fIWHEN\fR ", " \-\-no\-color
Control diagnostic color output (\fIauto\fR, \fIalways\fR, \fInever\fR).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress informational messages.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose transport diagnostics.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version and exit.
.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS
Press \fBCtrl+Alt+G\fR while streaming to toggle exclusive input capture.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean exit.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime, discovery, authentication, or connection error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage.
